{
 "source": "geneva",
 "book": "1KI",
 "chapter": 3,
 "units": [
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.3.1",
   "range": "1KI.3.1",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "770e7eff",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.3.1#p1-770e7eff",
     "text": "Which was Bethlehem.",
     "label": "a",
     "anchor": "city of David"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.3.2",
   "range": "1KI.3.2",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "41c10c37",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.3.2#p1-41c10c37",
     "text": "Where altars were appointed before the temple was built, to offer to the Lord.",
     "label": "b",
     "anchor": "high places"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.3.3",
   "range": "1KI.3.3",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "1d3099d3",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.3.3#p1-1d3099d3",
     "text": "For his father had commanded him to obey the Lord and walk in his ways, 1Ki 2:3.",
     "label": "c",
     "anchor": "father",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Ki 2:3",
       "ref": "1KI.2.3"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.3.4",
   "range": "1KI.3.4",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "1924754e",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.3.4#p1-1924754e",
     "text": "For there the tabernacle was 2Ch 1:3.",
     "label": "d",
     "anchor": "Gibeon to sacrifice there",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "2Ch 1:3",
       "ref": "2CH.1.3"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.3.6",
   "range": "1KI.3.6",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "2f8eb0d0",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.3.6#p1-2f8eb0d0",
     "text": "You have performed your promise.",
     "label": "e",
     "anchor": "kept for him this great kindness"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.3.7",
   "range": "1KI.3.7",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "c35d6bd5",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.3.7#p1-c35d6bd5",
     "text": "That is, to behave himself in executing this charge of ruling.",
     "label": "f",
     "anchor": "go out or come in"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.3.9",
   "range": "1KI.3.9",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "f9120e64",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.3.9#p1-f9120e64",
     "text": "Which are so many in number.",
     "label": "g",
     "anchor": "great a people"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.3.11",
   "range": "1KI.3.11",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "588d75ca",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.3.11#p1-588d75ca",
     "text": "That is, that their enemy would die.",
     "label": "h",
     "anchor": "enemies"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.3.15",
   "range": "1KI.3.15",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "1c48a298",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.3.15#p1-1c48a298",
     "text": "He knew that God had appeared to him in a dream.",
     "label": "i",
     "anchor": "a dream"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.3.16",
   "range": "1KI.3.16",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "85a3519d",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.3.16#p1-85a3519d",
     "text": "By this example it appears that God kept his promise to Solomon in granting him wisdom.",
     "label": "k",
     "anchor": "stood before him"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.3.20",
   "range": "1KI.3.20",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "c09027b6",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.3.20#p1-c09027b6",
     "text": "She stole the living child to avoid both the shame and punishment.",
     "label": "l",
     "anchor": "took my son from beside me"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.3.24",
   "range": "1KI.3.24",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "c5108ccd",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.3.24#p1-c5108ccd",
     "text": "Unless God gives judges understanding, the impudency of the trespasser will overthrow the just cause of the innocent.",
     "label": "m",
     "anchor": "Bring me a sword"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1KI.3.26",
   "range": "1KI.3.26",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "ad46f90c",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1KI.3.26#p1-ad46f90c",
     "text": "Her motherly affection appears in that she would rather endure the rigor of the law than see her child cruelly slain.",
     "label": "n",
     "anchor": "in no wise slay it"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
